# Agent behaviour

Read [`docs/working_agreement.md`](../../docs/working_agreement.md) before doing anything.
If this rule conflicts with that document, the working agreement wins.

**Doc hierarchy:** Repo docs (`working_agreement.md`, `engineering_standards.md`, `layering.md`)
override generic dbt or SQLFluff examples. Do not justify skipping §1.1 SQL structure
(models or singular tests) by citing "dbt standard" or community shortcuts.

## Permission to act

- Do not edit files, run terminal commands, or start implementation unless the user
  clearly asked for that action or replied with an explicit go-ahead after options were presented.
- When in doubt, ask one short clarifying question instead of acting.

## Before non-trivial changes

State one short block: **intent → files/systems touched → definition of done.**
If anything could silently shrink scope, stop and ask.

## Branches — always

Every change goes on a new branch. Never commit directly to `main`. Open a PR; wait for
CI and user approval before merging.

After the user merges, follow [`agent-pr-workflow.mdc`](agent-pr-workflow.mdc) **After merge**:
sync local `main` and delete merged branches without asking the user to do it.

## Layer contract (non-negotiable)

| Layer | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `1_staging` | Source-near cleanup only. No business logic. |
| `2_base` | Union and dedup across sources. |
| `3_core` | Canonical dimensions and facts. System of record. |
| `4_intermediate` | Complex logic reused by multiple marts. |
| `5_marts` | Consumption layer for app, export, or BI. |

Full rules: [`docs/layering.md`](../../docs/layering.md).

## Quality and communication

Follow [`docs/working_agreement.md`](../../docs/working_agreement.md) §4–§7 and
[`docs/engineering_standards.md`](../../docs/engineering_standards.md) §3 (testing).

